1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,490
Cleopatra lived closer to the Moon
landing than to the building of the Great

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,510
Pyramid. That is how old Egypt is.

3
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:11,340
Around 3100 BC, a king named Narmer united
Upper and Lower Egypt into one kingdom.

4
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:15,240
Every summer the Nile flooded, and the
black mud it left behind fed a whole

5
00:00:15,190 --> 00:00:19,960
civilization. Pharaohs were treated as
living gods, and gods need very big tombs.

6
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:22,740
The Great Pyramid used about
2.3 million stone blocks.

7
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:26,280
And archaeologists think it was
built by paid workers, not slaves.

8
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:30,790
Then foreign kings seized the north, riding
a terrifying new weapon: the horse-drawn

9
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:34,900
chariot. So Egypt copied the chariots, kicked
the invaders out, and built an empire.

10
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,610
Ramesses the Great ruled for 66 years.

11
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,110
But empires get tired.

12
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:42,350
Libyans, Nubians, Persians and
Greeks took turns on the throne.

13
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:46,020
The last ruling pharaoh was Cleopatra,
and when she died, Rome took Egypt.

14
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,570
Within a few centuries, nobody
on Earth could read hieroglyphs.

15
00:00:49,730 --> 00:00:52,440
For fourteen centuries, Egypt's
writing was a total mystery.

16
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:56,480
Until one stone with three scripts cracked
the code, and we finally learned how old

17
00:00:56,430 --> 00:00:57,400
Egypt really is.
